<article class="env-example" id="9B9FC6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/9B9FC6">Example <span data-tag="9B9FC6">8.2.9.5</span>.</a> The category $\cDelta $ of combinatorial simplices is a Reedy category with respect to the factorization system $( \cDelta ^{L}, \cDelta ^{R} )$; here a morphism $f: [m] \rightarrow [n]$ belongs to $\cDelta ^{L}$ if and only if $f$ is surjective, and to $\cDelta ^{R}$ if and only if $f$ is injective. </p>
